  "description": "A parametric TOWEL RACK on the six-node spine — Geometry → Input Properties → Math Engine → Output Metrics → 2D Render + 3D Render.\n\nSEGMENT-HOSTED AND ALMOST NOTHING IN PLAN, which is the honest symbol: a towel rail projects 80 mm and its plan is a sliver on the wall face. Drop it on a wall and it takes the wall's line.\n\nTHREE ARRANGEMENTS. Single is one rail between two brackets; Double adds a second lower rail; Ring drops both rails and the second bracket for a 24-point ring on one bracket. The towel hangs off whichever rail exists and empties for the ring, because a towel over a ring is a different drape and drawing it as a flat panel would be a lie.\n\nHANGING LENGTH is published — the rail run, doubled for two rails or 2πr for the ring — because that, not the width, is how much towel the thing actually takes.",
